        <body>
            <div xml:id="d554">

                <pb facs="1030" n="906" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg906"/>

                <head>No. 550.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Christiancy to Mr.
                    Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 8, 1881</date>.
                        (Received June 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 295.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to you the copy
                    of a letter from B. H. Kauffmann, our consular agent at Pacasmayo, dated May 5,
                    1881, in reference to the attempt of the Peruvian authorities to levy war
                    contributions upon American citizens, and their conclusion to desist from that
                    attempt.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>I. P. CHRISTIANCY.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d554-a1.xml" xpointer="d554-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
